  "text": "[GOTCHA] rebuild_state required after bulk create_track — `update_track_field` returns \"track not found\" on freshly created tracks. Always run `rebuild_state` MCP before any field updates on newly created tracks, or the updates silently fail.\n\n[GOTCHA] Write tool requires prior Read on the target path in the current session — the harness blocks Write until Read has been called. For partial changes use Edit instead (no Read requirement, matches on unique strings).\n\n[GOTCHA] Track frontmatter validation fires on Write but NOT on Edit — if you Write a track file, it must include `status:` in frontmatter or the PostToolUse hook blocks the operation. Edit modifications are exempt from this check.\n\n[GOTCHA] update_track_field rejects illegal status transitions (e.g. \"In Progress\" → \"In Progress\"). Use `force=true` only for cache recovery, never to bypass workflow rules. A 422 here usually means a sequencing error, not a tool bug.\n\n[GOTCHA] No alter/character names in Suno metatags — descriptive form `[male mid-baritone, weary, dry close-mic]` is permitted; character form `[Container]` is forbidden per voice-craft-principles.md. The rule is: describe the voice, never name the alter.",
